WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.345 --> 00:00:03.728
(relaxing music)

00:00:03.728 --> 00:00:06.253
- [Tyler] To be able to be
doing science while you're out

00:00:06.253 --> 00:00:09.553
there on the surfboard surfing
down the face of a wave,

00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:10.943
it's just such a fleeting moment.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:14.239
It's incredible to
actually be able to do it.

00:00:14.239 --> 00:00:16.822
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.097
- A Smartfin is a surfboard fin.

00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:25.171
You clip it on the bottom of your board

00:00:25.171 --> 00:00:28.229
and you go out for your surf session.

00:00:28.229 --> 00:00:32.245
It has technology that
measures ocean pH salinity,

00:00:32.245 --> 00:00:35.861
ocean temperature, and very
detailed wave characteristics.

00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:39.528
So there will be an
enormous amount of data.

00:00:40.476 --> 00:00:43.916
The reason these parameters
are important is because

00:00:43.916 --> 00:00:48.083
they are shifting directly as
a result of climate change.

00:00:49.241 --> 00:00:51.763
We get detailed information
about the deep ocean

00:00:51.763 --> 00:00:56.324
but very limited accurate
information about the near shore.

00:00:56.324 --> 00:00:58.462
Satellites can't be really accurate

00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:00.350
with data in that narrow zone.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.902
And the other way is ocean buoys

00:01:01.902 --> 00:01:04.893
and they're just not
deployed at the coast.

00:01:04.893 --> 00:01:07.726
Bingo, Smartfin can fill that gap.

00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:13.858
- Collecting oceanic data is a very

00:01:13.858 --> 00:01:17.382
time consuming, expensive process.

00:01:17.382 --> 00:01:20.582
This is like, you just
need to know how to surf.

00:01:20.582 --> 00:01:24.260
The data moves from your fin
to your phone via Bluetooth.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.228
And then from your phone
it goes up to our servers

00:01:26.228 --> 00:01:28.525
where everything's processed.

00:01:28.525 --> 00:01:31.803
I had to develop sensors that
don't affect the surfboard.

00:01:31.803 --> 00:01:36.239
Nobody's gonna surf a fin
that is not a standard foil.

00:01:36.239 --> 00:01:38.237
Aside from that LED right
there that's blinking

00:01:38.237 --> 00:01:40.058
that tells you that there's like

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:41.057
some sort of technology in there,

00:01:41.057 --> 00:01:43.807
you wouldn't know the difference.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:47.251
So we've got a test tank set up now.

00:01:47.251 --> 00:01:50.018
And we're just trying
to look at the precision

00:01:50.018 --> 00:01:53.243
and accuracy of the, um, instrument itself.

00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:56.243
Things are looking pretty promising.

00:01:57.123 --> 00:02:00.250
As a scientist it's pretty
exciting to be able to get data

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.307
over these different
time and space scales.

00:02:04.307 --> 00:02:06.329
I mean the fact that
you can go out and surf

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:08.481
and contribute to understanding

00:02:08.481 --> 00:02:12.993
what's actually happening
out there is incredible.

00:02:12.993 --> 00:02:15.647
- I'm not a surfer, I know
nothing about surfing.

00:02:15.647 --> 00:02:19.684
I know I look like a surfer, but I'm not.

00:02:19.684 --> 00:02:21.907
Surfers are very influential

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:24.467
and care deeply about the environment

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.634
and want to be talking about it.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.834
So Smartfin is just a tool to do that

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.834
in a more concrete way.

